    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nThe faces of a polyhedron are the polygonal sides that construct it.\n\nContent:\nLet's consider the triangular prism below.\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/a0d7b36cb7c8a69efbbc01beb1638a52]\n\nContent:\nOur triangular prism has [MATH: 5] faces:\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/9b04d849605bbe69f1307517a503d456]\n\nContent:\nThe vertices of a polyhedron are its corners. Our triangular prism has [MATH: 6] vertices:\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/ade61275401f006641b5b60d5c68f711]\n\nContent:\nThe edges of a polyhedron are the straight line segments that connect its vertices. Our triangular prism has [MATH: 9] edges:\n\nGraphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/9f65b8e71baf9f96ab67ec7ffc65889a]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Counting the Number of Faces of a Polyhedron\n\nExample Prompt:\nHow many faces does the cube shown below have?\n\n[IMG: /graphics/ace9fec3abdc83de3759bb06b534406b]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nThe cube has [MATH: 6] square faces:\n\n[IMG: /graphics/737c176bd7c337b744da64fc22146276]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nQuestion Graphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/q-61802]\n\nPrompt:\nHow many faces does the rectangular pyramid shown above have?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 4]\nb. [MATH: 5]\nc. [MATH: 3]\nd. [MATH: 8]\ne. [MATH: 6]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nQuestion Graphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/q-61806]\n\nPrompt:\nHow many faces does the rectangular prism shown above have?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 12]\nb. [MATH: 8]\nc. [MATH: 10]\nd. [MATH: 6]\ne. [MATH: 4]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Counting the Number of Vertices of a Polyhedron\n\nExample Prompt:\nHow many vertices does the rectangular prism shown below have?\n\n[IMG: /graphics/96e9414f2571c87c3cd9aed9e8a945fd]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nThe vertices of a polyhedron are the corners where edges meet.\n\nThe rectangular prism has [MATH: 8] vertices in total, as shown below.\n\n[IMG: /graphics/28197aed688da15174538ddf5856c0f3]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nQuestion Graphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/q-61786]\n\nPrompt:\nHow many vertices does the hexagonal pyramid shown above have?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 6]\nb. [MATH: 8]\nc. [MATH: 12]\nd. [MATH: 7]\ne. [MATH: 10]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nQuestion Graphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/q-61788]\n\nPrompt:\nHow many vertices does the triangular pyramid shown above have?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 6]\nb. [MATH: 4]\nc. [MATH: 3]\nd. [MATH: 5]\ne. [MATH: 9]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Counting the Number of Edges of a Polyhedron\n\nExample Prompt:\nHow many edges does the triangular pyramid shown below have?\n\n[IMG: /graphics/96c94b3d2fd3d11f5763882876817c8b]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nEdges are straight line segments that connect the vertices of a polyhedron.\n\nThe triangular pyramid has [MATH: 6] edges in total, as shown below.\n\n[IMG: /graphics/fee6835e24993eae604782dc1008df6a]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nQuestion Graphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/q-61552]\n\nPrompt:\nHow many edges does the rectangular pyramid shown above have?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 8]\nb. [MATH: 7]\nc. [MATH: 9]\nd. [MATH: 6]\ne. [MATH: 5]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nQuestion Graphic:\n[IMG: /graphics/q-61796]\n\nPrompt:\nHow many edges does the pentagonal prism shown above have?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 25]\nb. [MATH: 15]\nc. [MATH: 20]\nd. [MATH: 18]\ne. [MATH: 12]"
